infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Constant default vs volatile default on PG 11+
  desc The one question to ask of any ADD COLUMN: is the default a literal or a function call?
  compares
    - label Constant default ('pending', 42)
      children
        - label Instant (milliseconds)
          desc Catalog update only — no rows touched, any table size
        - label Stored in pg_attribute
          desc atthasmissing = true, attmissingval = the default
        - label Synthesised at read time
          desc Old rows keep their storage; value injected on SELECT
    - label Volatile default (now(), uuid())
      children
        - label Minutes per 100M rows
          desc Full heap rewrite under AccessExclusiveLock
        - label Materialised per row
          desc Each row needs a distinct value — no single missing value fits
        - label Safe fix is three steps
          desc Add no-default column, batch-backfill, then SET DEFAULT
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
